AWARD SYSTEM DOCUMENTATION
==========================
Project: Wiifarm / Food MLM Platform
Last updated: 2026-07-08


────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
1. OVERVIEW
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

The Award System recognises and rewards members who accumulate Point
Values (PV) on both legs of their binary MLM tree. When a user's
left-leg PV and right-leg PV reach the thresholds defined on an
Award, that Award is automatically granted and the user becomes
eligible for a cash payment from the admin.

Key principles:
  • Awards are never granted in real-time. Qualification is checked
    nightly by a scheduled cron job that dispatches one background
    job per eligible user.
  • Each Award is earned only once per user (unique constraint on
    user_awards.user_id + award_id).
  • Awards can be chained: an Award may require a Prerequisite Award
    to exist on each leg of the user's binary sub-tree before it
    can be earned.
  • Payment is manual: an admin reviews the user_awards table and
    approves the cash payment. Once paid, the amount is credited to
    the user's `awards` wallet column, from which the user can
    transfer it to their main balance (Money Box).


────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
2. DATABASE SCHEMA
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

2.1  awards  (migration: 2026_07_07_100001_create_awards_table.php)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Column                 Type              Notes
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  id                     bigint PK
  name                   varchar(150)      Unique. Display name of the award.
  description            text nullable     Shown to users on the My Awards page.
  required_total_pv      decimal(12,2)     Sum of left+right PV that must be met.
  required_left_pv       decimal(12,2)     Minimum PV in the left leg.
  required_right_pv      decimal(12,2)     Minimum PV in the right leg.
  prerequisite_award_id  bigint nullable   FK → awards.id (ON DELETE SET NULL).
                                           See Section 3.4 for full explanation.
  payment_amount         decimal(12,2)     Cash amount credited to user on payment.
  image                  varchar nullable  Stored at assets/images/awards/ (200×200 px).
  sort_order             uint              Controls display order (ascending).
  status                 tinyint           1 = active, 0 = inactive.
                                           Only active awards are evaluated by the job.
  created_at / updated_at

2.2  user_awards  (migration: 2026_07_07_100002_create_user_awards_table.php)
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Column        Type               Notes
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  id            bigint PK
  user_id       bigint FK → users
  award_id      bigint FK → awards
  status        tinyint            0 = earned / awaiting payment
                                   1 = paid
  earned_at     timestamp nullable  When the job created this record.
  paid_at       timestamp nullable  When the admin approved payment.
  paid_by       bigint nullable     admin.id who processed the payment.
  paid_amount   decimal(12,2)      Actual amount paid (snapshot of award.payment_amount).
  note          text nullable       Admin note recorded at payment time.
  created_at / updated_at

  Unique constraint: (user_id, award_id) — one row per user per award.

2.3  users.awards  (migration: 2026_07_07_100003_add_awards_wallet_to_users_table.php)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Column   Type             Notes
  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  awards   decimal(15,2)    Wallet balance credited by admin payments.
                            User can transfer this to balance (Money Box)
                            via the Bonus Transfer page.


────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
3. QUALIFICATION LOGIC  (CheckUserAwardJob)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

File: core/app/Jobs/CheckUserAwardJob.php
Dispatched by: core/app/Console/Commands/CheckAwardQualifications.php

The job evaluates a single user against every active Award in
sort_order / required_total_pv ascending order. It uses the user's
STAGE-1 Matrix entry, which holds the cumulative PV counters.

3.1  Eligibility pre-conditions
────────────────────────────────
  • The user must have profile_complete = 1.
  • The user must have a Matrix record where stage_id = 1.
    (This is the binary placement matrix used for pairing PV.)

3.2  PV source
───────────────
  Left PV  = Matrix.pv_left_pairing   (cumulative PV from all users
  Right PV = Matrix.pv_right_pairing   placed in each leg)
  Total PV = left_pv + right_pv

3.3  Per-award checks (in this exact order)
────────────────────────────────────────────
  a. Skip if the user already has a UserAward record for this award.
  b. Left PV  >= award.required_left_pv       — fail → skip this award.
  c. Right PV >= award.required_right_pv      — fail → skip this award.
  d. Total PV >= award.required_total_pv      — fail → skip this award.
  e. Prerequisite check (only if prerequisite_award_id is set)
     — see Section 3.4.
  f. All checks pass → create UserAward(status=0, earned_at=now()).
     The new award_id is immediately added to the in-memory earned list
     so later awards in the same job run can chain off it.

3.4  Prerequisite Award (leg-inheritance check)
─────────────────────────────────────────────────
  When an Award has a prerequisite_award_id set, the user cannot earn
  it unless a member in EACH leg of their binary sub-tree has already
  earned that prerequisite award.

  Algorithm:
    i.  Get the user's direct left child (Matrix.left) and right child
        (Matrix.right) from their stage-1 matrix row.
    ii. If either child slot is empty (null), the leg is not built —
        skip this award.
   iii. Run BFS (breadth-first search) starting from the left child to
        collect all user_ids in the left sub-tree (capped at 1,000).
    iv. Run BFS starting from the right child for the right sub-tree.
     v. Check user_awards for prerequisite_award_id in the left set.
    vi. Check user_awards for prerequisite_award_id in the right set.
   vii. Both must exist — if either leg is missing the prerequisite,
        skip this award.

  BFS implementation detail (getLegUserIds):
    • Processes 100 users at a time (array_splice batching).
    • Queries Matrix WHERE stage_id=1 AND parent_id IN (batch IDs)
      to find children.
    • Hard cap: 1,000 users per leg to prevent runaway queries on
      large trees.


────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
4. CRON JOB
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

File:     core/routes/console.php
Command:  award:check-qualifications
Class:    core/app/Console/Commands/CheckAwardQualifications.php

Schedule definition:
  Schedule::command('award:check-qualifications')
      ->dailyAt('02:00')
      ->withoutOverlapping()
      ->runInBackground()
      ->appendOutputTo(storage_path('logs/award-check.log'));

  Runs at:         02:00 server time, every day.
  Overlap guard:   withoutOverlapping() — if a previous run is still
                   active, the new invocation is skipped automatically.
  Background:      runInBackground() — does not block the scheduler
                   process.
  Log file:        storage/logs/award-check.log

What the command does:
  1. Queries Matrix WHERE stage_id = 1 to get the set of user_ids
     that are actually in the binary placement matrix.
  2. Queries User WHERE profile_complete = 1 AND id IN (matrix users),
     selecting only the id column.
  3. Chunks the result in batches of 200.
  4. For each user, dispatches CheckUserAwardJob::dispatch($user->id).
  5. Prints a dot (.) per chunk and reports total dispatched count.

The jobs then run asynchronously via Laravel's queue. Configure the
queue worker to process the default queue:

  php artisan queue:work --sleep=3 --tries=3 --max-time=3600

Job settings:
  public int $tries   = 3;    // retried up to 3 times on failure
  public int $timeout = 120;  // single job execution limit in seconds

Server cron entry (required for the Laravel scheduler to fire):
  * * * * * cd /path/to/project/core && php artisan schedule:run >> /dev/null 2>&1


────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
5. AWARD CONFIGURATION (ADMIN)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Routes (all prefixed admin/ and require admin auth):
  GET    admin/awards                → List all awards
  GET    admin/awards/create         → Create form
  POST   admin/awards/store          → Save new award
  GET    admin/awards/edit/{award}   → Edit form
  POST   admin/awards/update/{award} → Update award
  POST   admin/awards/toggle/{award} → Activate / deactivate (AJAX)
  DELETE admin/awards/{award}        → Delete award + image
  GET    admin/awards/payments       → Payment list (filterable by status)
  POST   admin/awards/pay/{userAward}→ Process a single payment

Controller: core/app/Http/Controllers/Admin/AwardController.php

5.1  Creating / Editing an Award
──────────────────────────────────
  Field              Validation
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  name               required, string, max:150, unique (excluding self on edit)
  description        nullable, string
  required_total_pv  required, numeric, min:0
  required_left_pv   required, numeric, min:0
  required_right_pv  required, numeric, min:0
  prerequisite_award_id  nullable, must exist in awards.id
                     Empty string from the HTML select is coerced to
                     null before fill() to avoid FK constraint errors.
  payment_amount     required, numeric, min:0
  image              nullable, image file, jpeg/png/jpg/gif, max 2 MB
                     Stored at: assets/images/awards/ (200×200 px)
  sort_order         required, integer, min:0
  status             required, 0 or 1

5.2  Toggling Active / Inactive
────────────────────────────────
  POST admin/awards/toggle/{award} flips status between 0 and 1.
  Returns JSON { success: true }.
  Inactive awards are excluded from the nightly qualification check
  (Award::active() scope → WHERE status = 1).

5.3  Processing a Payment
──────────────────────────
  POST admin/awards/pay/{userAward}
  Runs inside DB::transaction:
    1. user->awards  +=  award.payment_amount     (increment wallet)
    2. user_awards row updated:
         status      = 1
         paid_at     = now()
         paid_by     = auth('admin')->id()
         paid_amount = award.payment_amount
         note        = request.note (optional)

  After payment, the `awards` column on the users table holds the
  credited amount. The user transfers it to their Money Box via the
  Bonus Transfer page (see Section 7).

5.4  Deleting an Award
───────────────────────
  DELETE admin/awards/{award}
  Removes the image file from disk before deleting the database row.
  The FK on prerequisite_award_id is ON DELETE SET NULL, so child
  awards that referenced this award as a prerequisite will have their
  prerequisite_award_id set to null automatically.


────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
6. USER-FACING AWARD PAGE
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Route:      GET user/awards   → name: user.awards
Controller: PlanController@myAwards
View:       core/resources/views/templates/basic/user/awards.blade.php
Sidebar:    Achievements → My Awards (Finance accordion group)

What the page shows:
  • A hero strip with counters: total awards, earned, paid.
  • One card per active Award (sorted by sort_order).
  • Card states:
      locked  — user has not earned this award (greyscale, grey ring)
      earned  — earned but not yet paid (green, animated pulse badge)
      paid    — payment received (gold gradient)
  • Earned date or paid date shown at the card footer.
  • The sidebar badge on "My Awards" shows the count of earned-but-
    unpaid awards (UserAward WHERE user_id = auth AND status = 0).

Data loading:
  $allAwards  = Award::active()->orderBy('sort_order')->get();
  $earnedMap  = UserAward::where('user_id', $user->id)->get()->keyBy('award_id');

Card state detection:
  $earned   = $earnedMap->get($award->id);
  $isPaid   = $earned && $earned->status == 1;
  $isEarned = $earned && !$isPaid;
  $isLocked = !$earned;


────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
7. AWARDS WALLET & BONUS TRANSFER
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

After an admin payment is processed, the cash is held in the
`users.awards` decimal column. This is separate from the user's
main `balance` (Money Box).

To move it into the Money Box the user visits:
  GET user/bonus-transfer   → BonusTransferController@index

Awards is one of six transferable bonus types:
  direct_bonus, indirect_bonus, upgrade_bonus,
  unilevel_bonus, awards, pairing_bonus

Transfer flow:
  1. User clicks "Transfer" on the Awards row.
  2. An authorization modal appears asking for the account password.
  3. On submit:
       POST user/bonus-transfer/transfer
       { bonus_field: "awards", amount: <n>, password: <pw> }
  4. Server validates password with Hash::check.
  5. DB::transaction:
       user.awards   -= amount
       user.balance  += amount
       Transaction record created (trx_type='+', remark='bonus_transfer',
         details='Bonus Transfer from Awards', bonus_type=6,
         post_balance=user.balance after credit)
       Transfer record created (STATUS_COMPLETED)


────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
8. MODELS & RELATIONSHIPS
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Award  (core/app/Models/Award.php)
  fillable:      name, description, required_total_pv, required_left_pv,
                 required_right_pv, prerequisite_award_id, payment_amount,
                 image, sort_order, status
  relationships: prerequisite() → belongsTo(Award, prerequisite_award_id)
                 userAwards()   → hasMany(UserAward)
  scopes:        active()       → where('status', 1)
  accessor:      $award->image_url → full URL at assets/images/awards/

UserAward  (core/app/Models/UserAward.php)
  fillable:      user_id, award_id, status, earned_at, paid_at,
                 paid_by, paid_amount, note
  relationships: user()  → belongsTo(User)
                 award() → belongsTo(Award)
  scopes:        pending() → where('status', 0)
                 paid()    → where('status', 1)


